A command whose broken holds a type error, and an ignore file whose entries name
broken: one with no reason, one with no path, one complete. A refused entry is a row
of the ignore file, so DS9001 and DS9002 are reported although the type error skips
broken, and the complete entry, which matches no finding, is stale.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

func broken() int { return undefinedName }
-- deadset-ignore.json --
{"ignore": [
  {"code": "DS1002", "symbol": "go://example.com/app#broken", "path": "main.go"},
  {"code": "DS1002", "symbol": "go://example.com/app#broken", "reason": "kept"},
  {"code": "DS1002", "symbol": "go://example.com/app#broken", "path": "main.go", "reason": "kept for the loader"}
]}
